write('MATHEMATICAL_EXPLANATION_AUDIT.md','# Mathematical explanation audit\n\nAll four original mathematical lines are byte-identical and retain native OMML rendering.\n\n1. Equation 1: T2 is introduced as a numerical reference at first body use. ANSYS elastic stress recovery precedes tensile maximum-principal clipping and original-area averaging. Same-face 1 mm Euclidean chord support, radius tolerance and coverage remain unchanged. No geodesic, fatigue standard or physical gauge is substituted.\n2. Equation 2: normalized L2 is introduced as relative whole-field discrepancy, dimensionless, lower-is-better, not average pointwise percentage error or a location metric. Original weights and denominator remain exact.\n3. Equation 3: MAE is explained immediately before its formula as original-area-weighted average absolute numerical error in MPa.\n4. Equation 4: RMSE is explained immediately before its formula as a measure emphasizing large deviations, in MPa, not measurement uncertainty.\n\nThe eight-cell experiment is explained before contrast scaling, whose exact original convention remains in Supplementary Readability Method Notes A5. Stability, signed bias, peak/Q95 differences, High95, rank masks, common thresholds, empty-mask handling and equal-plate aggregation retain their original operators and qualifications. New formulae or thresholds were not introduced.\n')
write('SCIENCE_PRESERVATION_AUDIT.md','# Science preservation audit\n\nPASS. The independent structural/content checks are in QA/SCIENCE_PRESERVATION_CHECKS.csv. This is an editorial preservation check, not new FE, ML or statistical research.\n\nSeven original numerical tables, four mathematical lines, nine image links, every main/SI image file and all sixteen references are unchanged. Original author declarations and availability statements are unchanged except expansion of CPU in Code availability. Citation first-appearance order remains 1–16. All original numeric tokens remain in the revised main article plus explicitly referenced notes; exact tables, original claim ledgers and retained paragraphs provide the necessary comparison context beyond token coverage. Fifteen relocated passages are preserved in the notes, including exact loading/gauges, optimizer/sampling settings, contrast scaling, quota handling and secondary adverse findings.\n\nThirteen sources, five documentary plate groups, two fixed seeds, 100 MPa reference load, E = 210 GPa, Poisson ratio 0.30, T2 operator, original area weighting, architecture and training settings remain fixed. Negative X outcomes, extreme common-threshold deterioration, peak-error worsening, local/whole-field trade-offs, missing restricted geometry comparators and physical/cohort limitations remain explicit. METHOD_IMPROVEMENT_MIXED is unchanged.\n\nWording risks corrected: local-input observability is not prediction invariance; higher IoU is not amplitude validation; a stable output may be inaccurate; a better oracle score does not recover missing geometry operationally; G1 superiority does not establish neural necessity; documentary plates are not independently certified batches. No new physical mechanism, experimental stress accuracy, fatigue life, crack detection or industrial readiness is claimed. No solver, model, fit, inference, threshold study or numerical experiment was run.\n')
write('MANUSCRIPT_READABILITY_CHANGELOG.md','# Manuscript readability changelog\n\nThe latest verified visual release is used unchanged as the scientific baseline. The article now defines measurement/model assumptions, representation and observation context before specialist details; explains T2, field error, localization and thresholds at first substantive use; distinguishes the N1/N2/N3 purposes; motivates the controlled substitutions before factorial language; and states findings before numerical support. Discussion and conclusions synthesize the numerical trade-offs. Captions identify what each color/quantity means. Fifteen detailed passages are relocated, not discarded, into named supplementary notes.\n\nThe main manuscript contains no local machine paths. Original figures, table data, equations, references, SI references, adverse findings and author-confirmation placeholders remain. Research is closed and the classification remains METHOD_IMPROVEMENT_MIXED.\n\n'+f'{len(changes)} paragraph-level changes are recorded in QA/EDITORIAL_CHANGE_RECORDS.json. Full before/after text and relocation references are available for author inspection.\n')
write('FINAL_AUTHOR_REVIEW_CHECKLIST.md','# Final author review checklist\n\n1. Review the revised scientific wording and fifteen supplementary-note references; confirm that explanations preserve the intended methods and limits.\n2. Confirm authors, affiliations, contributions, funding, interests, permissions and all retained placeholders before submission.\n3. Approve the complete AI-assisted research, writing and figure-production history and human scientific responsibility.\n4. Verify the current official JCSR article, abstract, length, anonymity, artwork and upload-size rules. Previous journal-specific access was incomplete; no new mandatory limit is invented here.\n5. Review the Word-generated PDF and full-width figure placement. All scientific images remain unchanged; dense SI grids retain original artwork for zoom.\n6. Decide and document actual derived-data/code availability and third-party permissions. Provenance CSVs retain historical paths and require privacy review for public or anonymous use.\n7. Reconcile the final portal file inventory, cover letter, highlights and declarations with the revised text, then approve the portal-generated PDF.\n\nThe package is ready for private author review, not an author-approved automatic journal submission. No upload, publication, license selection, fee payment or public deposit has occurred.\n')

